{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For you were sore longing for your father's house.</b> The duplication of expression alludes that he longed for his father and longed for the Holy Land, in the manner of (Psalms 84:3): ״נכספה וגם כלתה נפשי לחצרות אלהי״." "<b>And it is fitting</b> to say that the added ה״י (the letter heh) alludes to the Glory (כבוד) concerning which it is written (Isaiah 64:10): ״בית קדשנו ותפארתנו״ — 'our holy house and our glory.' And it was to this that he longed, for בית קדשנו is the Glory, and תפארתנו is the Tif'eret of Israel. And it is written (Psalms 96:6): ״עוז ותפארת במקדשו״ — understand this. And whoever does not long for it is the sinner. And in this same expression we find that the prophet rebuked Israel when they did not long for the fear of HaShem and the observance of His commandments, as he said (Zephaniah 2:1): ״התקוששו וקושו הגוי לא נכסף״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "The added letter heh refers to the heh appended to the verb נכסף in Genesis 31:30 (נכספתה vs. standard נכספת)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:41.826627542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}